# Ownership record for the paper trail. Solo repo — the owner owns everything.
#
# Practical effect, so nobody re-derives it later:
#
#   - Your own PRs get NO review request. GitHub never requests a review from a
#     PR's own author, even when that author is the code owner. This file is
#     inert on self-authored PRs.
#   - Dependabot PRs (author: dependabot[bot]) DO trigger a review request to
#     @Damilss, on every weekly npm and github-actions batch. That is the one
#     real behavior change.
#   - Do NOT enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection. It
#     can never be satisfied on your own PR — GitHub will not let you approve
#     yourself — so every solo merge would become an admin override, which turns
#     branch protection from a signal into noise you learn to click through.
#
# CODEOWNERS is read from the BASE branch of a PR, not the default branch.

* @Damilss
